0..79 Comment "// A source that performs the operation of an `extern` block in another source."
80..157 Comment "// `round-trip.gandr` declares the block `Boundary`, and this source declares"
158..170 Comment "// no block."
171..173 Comment "//"
174..252 Comment "// A program keeps its Rust boundary in one source. Each other source performs"
253..332 Comment "// the boundary\'s operations through an import of that source, and it writes no"
333..354 Comment "// copy of the block."
355..357 Comment "//"
358..435 Comment "// The import opens the block\'s interface. A row here names `Boundary`, and a"
436..508 Comment "// call performs `Boundary.add`. The run offers each perform to the Rust"
509..589 Comment "// caller\'s host, as it does for `quadrupled`. The block\'s row check runs at the"
590..618 Comment "// block\'s own source alone."
619..621 Comment "//"
622..691 Comment "// - see: `model/interop/boundary/round-trip.gandr` — the block and"
692..709 Comment "//   `quadrupled`"
710..785 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-dispatcher/tests/boundary.rs` — the Rust caller"
787..818 Comment "// `Boundary` and `quadrupled`."
